<html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><style>
body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#111827;line-height:1.7;max-width:860px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 28px}
h1{font-size:22pt;color:#111827;border-bottom:3px solid #c5a028;padding-bottom:8px;margin-bottom:4px}
h2{font-size:14pt;color:#111827;margin-top:30px;margin-bottom:4px;border-left:4px solid #4fd1c5;padding-left:12px;background:#f4fdfc}
h3{font-size:12pt;color:#374151;margin:16px 0 4px;font-weight:bold}
p{margin:4px 0 10px}
.meta{background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 18px;margin-bottom:24px;font-size:10pt}
.meta p{margin:3px 0}
.meta strong{color:#b7881c}
.sec{border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;margin-top:28px;padding-top:16px}
.badge{display:inline-block;background:#ecfdf5;color:#065f46;font-size:9pt;font-weight:bold;padding:3px 12px;border-radius:20px;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px}
.card{background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin:10px 0}
.card-title{font-weight:bold;font-size:11.5pt;color:#111827;margin:0 0 4px}
.card-sub{font-size:10pt;color:#6b7280;margin:0 0 4px;font-style:italic}
.card-desc{color:#374151;margin:0;font-size:10.5pt}
.step{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 14px;background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;margin:8px 0}
.step-num{font-size:18pt;font-weight:bold;color:#c5a028;min-width:40px;line-height:1}
.step-body .step-title{font-weight:bold;font-size:11pt;color:#111827;margin:0 0 3px}
.step-body .step-desc{font-size:10.5pt;color:#374151;margin:0}
.faq{border-left:3px solid #4fd1c5;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0;background:#f9fafb;border-radius:0 6px 6px 0}
.faq-q{font-weight:bold;color:#111827;margin:0 0 5px}
.faq-a{color:#374151;margin:0;font-size:10.5pt}
.cta{background:#111827;color:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:20px 24px;margin-top:28px}
.cta h2{color:#4fd1c5;border:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 8px;background:transparent;font-size:15pt}
.cta p{color:#d1d5db;margin:4px 0}
.cta .btn{display:inline-block;background:#4fd1c5;color:#111827;font-weight:bold;padding:7px 16px;border-radius:5px;margin-top:8px;font-size:10pt}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px 0;font-size:10.5pt}
td{padding:7px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb}
td:first-child{color:#6b7280}
td:last-child{font-weight:bold;color:#111827;text-align:right}
ul{padding-left:18px}
ul li{padding:2px 0;color:#374151}
</style></head><body><h1>Usda Loans</h1><div class="meta"><p><strong>Page Title:</strong> Map Address Eligibility</p><p><strong>Meta Description:</strong> USDA rural development loans in Wisconsin with zero down payment. Rob Miller helps families qualify for 100% financing in eligible areas. Licensed in 11 states. Call 608-227-2002.</p></div><div class="sec"><div class="badge">USDA Loan Program</div><br><h2>USDA Home Loans in Wisconsin</h2><p>100% financing with no down payment for eligible rural and suburban Wisconsin properties. USDA loans are one of the best-kept secrets in mortgage financing — offering competitive rates, low fees, and zero money down for buyers who qualify.</p><p><strong>CTA Button:</strong> Check USDA Eligibility</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>Process Roadmap</h2><div class="step"><div class="step-num">01</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Map Address Eligibility</p><p class="step-desc">Verify that your target home is located in an eligible rural/suburban census block (Verona, DeForest, etc.).</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">02</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Review Income Threshold</p><p class="step-desc">Check your total household income to ensure it is under the 115% area median income limit.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">03</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Get USDA Pre-Approval</p><p class="step-desc">Rob Miller reviews your credit profile (640+ preferred) to establish zero-down financing power.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">04</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">House Hunt</p><p class="step-desc">Shop for move-in ready properties in eligible Wisconsin communities with your real estate agent.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">05</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">USDA Guarantee Setup</p><p class="step-desc">We structure the loan with a low 1.0% upfront fee and 0.35% annual fee rolled into the mortgage.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">06</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Closing Day</p><p class="step-desc">Complete your final signatures, pay zero down payment, and take possession of your home.</p></div></div></div><div class="sec"><h2>Main Page Content</h2><h3>What Is a USDA Home Loan?</h3><h3>USDA Loan Benefits</h3><h3>Your USDA Loan Roadmap</h3><h3>USDA vs. FHA vs. VA: Which Is Right for You?</h3><h4>USDA Quick Facts</h4><p>A USDA loan is a government-backed mortgage program offered through the U.S. Department of Agriculture's Rural Development division. Despite the name, USDA loans are not just for farms or remote countryside — they cover a surprisingly broad range of suburban and small-city properties across Wisconsin.</p><p>The USDA Guaranteed Loan Program (Section 502) allows approved lenders like MadCity Home Loans to offer 100% financing to eligible borrowers purchasing in qualifying areas. The USDA guarantees a portion of the loan, allowing lenders to offer rates and terms comparable to conventional financing — with no down payment required.</p><p>For Wisconsin buyers who earn a moderate income and are purchasing outside major urban centers, USDA loans are often the most affordable path to homeownership available.</p><p>If you're eligible for USDA, it's often the best option for non-veterans buying in qualifying areas. USDA's annual fee (0.35%) is lower than FHA's annual MIP (0.55%), and USDA offers $0 down just like VA loans.</p><p>The key constraints are geographic eligibility and income limits. If your property or income doesn't qualify for USDA, FHA or conventional financing are natural alternatives.</p><p>Not sure if your property qualifies? Rob Miller can check your specific address against the USDA eligibility map in minutes — at no cost or obligation.</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>USDA Quick Facts</h2><table><tr><td>Down Payment</td><td>$0</td></tr><tr><td>Min. Credit Score</td><td>640</td></tr><tr><td>Upfront Fee</td><td>1.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Annual Fee</td><td>0.35%</td></tr><tr><td>Owner Occupied</td><td>Required</td></tr><tr><td>Income Limits</td><td>Yes</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><h2>USDA Loan FAQs — Wisconsin Homebuyers</h2><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What areas in Wisconsin are eligible for USDA loans?</p><p class="faq-a">A: USDA loan eligibility is based on population density, not whether land is "rural." Many Wisconsin suburbs and smaller cities qualify — including areas near Madison such as DeForest, Waunakee, Stoughton, and Verona (portions). You can check eligibility at the USDA's official map, or Rob Miller can verify your specific property address instantly.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: Is there really no down payment required for a USDA loan?</p><p class="faq-a">A: Yes — USDA loans offer 100% financing, meaning you can purchase a home with $0 down payment. This makes them one of the only zero-down mortgage options available today alongside VA loans.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What are the income limits for a USDA loan in Wisconsin?</p><p class="faq-a">A: USDA income limits vary by county and household size. For 2026, the standard limit for most Wisconsin counties is approximately $122,000 for 1-4 person households and $161,000 for 5-8 person households. These limits are higher than many people expect — about 115% of the area median income.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What is the USDA guarantee fee?</p><p class="faq-a">A: USDA loans charge a one-time upfront guarantee fee of 1.0% of the loan amount (vs. FHA's 1.75%) which can be rolled into the loan. There is also an annual fee of 0.35% of the outstanding balance, paid monthly. This is significantly lower than FHA's annual MIP, making USDA loans very cost-effective for eligible buyers.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What credit score is required for a USDA loan?</p><p class="faq-a">A: The USDA does not set a minimum credit score, but most lenders — including MadCity Home Loans — require a minimum score of 640 for the automated approval process. Borrowers with scores below 640 may still qualify through manual underwriting with compensating factors.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: Can I use a USDA loan to buy a fixer-upper?</p><p class="faq-a">A: The standard USDA Guaranteed Loan requires the home to be in move-in ready condition. However, the USDA 504 Repair program and USDA Section 502 Direct loans may provide options for repairs and renovations. Rob Miller can help you explore which program fits your situation.</p></div></div><div class="cta"><h2>Ready to Check Your USDA Eligibility?</h2><p>Rob Miller can verify your property address and income eligibility in minutes. Zero-down homeownership may be closer than you think.</p><span class="btn">Start My USDA Pre-Approval</span></div></body></html>